ury goods","desert_salt"],"recommended":[],"reasons":{"metals":"Riverside terrain cannot produce this locally","luxury goods":"Riverside terrain cannot produce this locally","desert_salt":"Required by Salt works but not available in Riverside terrain"}},"exports":[],"gaps":[{"chain":"stone","institution":"Stone quarry","kind":"missing","impact":"Stone quarry exists but lacks access to stone","severity":"high"},{"chain":"desert_salt","institution":"Salt works","kind":"imported","impact":"Salt works runs on imported desert_salt","severity":"low"},{"chain":"timber","institution":"Sawmill (commercial)","kind":"imported","impact":"Sawmill (commercial) runs on imported timber","severity":"low"},{"chain":"mountain_timber","institution":"Sawmill (commercial)","kind":"imported","impact":"Sawmill (commercial) runs on imported mountain_timber","severity":"low"},{"chain":"game","institution":"Hunter's lodge","kind":"missing","impact":"Hunter's lodge exists but lacks access to game","severity":"high"}],"featureEffects":[],"economicStrengths":["River trade"],"strategicValue":"Medium - controls river crossing and inland trade","priorityNotes":[]},"economicViability":{"viable":true,"issues":[],"warnings":[{"severity":"note","title":"Trade Dependencies","description":"8 institutions depend on imported materials (Trade access + grain, Trade access, Grain). Standard for this trade route: vulnerability if supply is disrupted."}],"dependencies":[],"suggestions":[{"category":"Resource Chain","title":"Incomplete chain: foraging_areas","description":"Processing foraging_areas but missing Elder Grove Council, Chandler, Midwife for the full chain.","impact":"Exports intermediate goods instead of final products (Honey and beeswax, Foraged goods, Wild honey, Candles and wax). Lower profit margins.","suggestedFixes":["Add Elder Grove Council and Chandler and Midwife to complete the production chain"]}],"plotHooks":[],"summary":"✓ VIABLE WITH PROVISIONING SUPPORT: imports, reserves, or extraordinary supply cover 2% of daily food need.","metrics":{"foodBalance":{"dailyNeed":2788,"dailyProduction":2735,"deficit":0,"deficitPercent":0,"surplus":0,"agricultureModifier":1.3900000000000001,"importCoverage":53,"rawDeficit":53,"importChannel":"river trade"},"tradeAccess":"river","criticalIssueCount":0,"dependencyCount":0,"warningCount":1}},"history":{"age":224,"founding":{"age":224,"reason":"started as a seasonal camp beside a dependable river fishery and became permanent when traders began stopping there","foundedBy":"a merchant consortium that needed a waypoint and decided to own it","initialChallenge":"seasonal flooding that destroyed early buildings","overcoming":"through determination and cooperation","stressNote":null},"historicalEvents":[{"yearsAgo":222,"type":"religious","name":"The Heresy Trials","description":"A charge of heresy laid against a well-known figure divided the faithful and pulled the secular powers in on either side of it","severity":"minor","lastingEffects":[],"plotHooks":[],"templateType":"heresy_trial"},{"yearsAgo":147,"type":"magical","name":"The Wild Magic","description":"An uncontrolled surge of magic left its mark on the waterfront and on the people who were there, and the effects have never fully faded","severity":"minor","lastingEffects":[],"plotHooks":[],"templateType":"wild_magic"},{"yearsAgo":116,"type":"disaster","name":"The Siege","description":"An approaching danger set the community against itself over the right response","severity":"major","lastingEffects":["A standing levy roster kept ready in the town archive"],"plotHooks":[],"templateType":"external_threat","anchored":true},{"yearsAgo":110,"type":"occupation_infiltration","name":"The Purge","description":"Fear of hidden infiltrators (not always unfounded) bred denunciations and a climate of mistrust","severity":"major","lastingEffects":["Denunciation records from the panic remain sealed in the archive"],"plotHooks":[],"templateType":"infiltration_fear","anchored":true},{"yearsAgo":58,"type":"exile_return","name":"The Occupation","description":"A previous occupation ended, but collaborators and resisters continued to live side by side, their history unresolved","severity":"major","lastingEffects":["Collaborator and resistance families still keep apart"],"plotHooks":["Resistance fighters kept records that would expose people still in power","Families who lived through it tell it this way: a former occupier officer has returned under a false identity"],"templateType":"occupation_legacy","anchored":true},{"yearsAgo":44,"type":"political","name":"The Tyranny","description":"One figure took power by economic pressure and held it unchecked for a season, and the memory still governs who the town will trust with authority","severity":"catastrophic","lastingEffects":[],"plotHooks":["The records of that time say: someone is deliberately rehabilitating the tyrant’s reputation, and profiting from it","An old story from that time: a fortune the regime confiscated was never returned, and the rightful heirs have surfaced"],"templateType":"tyranny"},{"yearsAgo":25,"type":"economic","name":"The Economic Divide","description":"A widening gulf between the well-off and the working poor breeds lasting resentment","severity":"major","lastingEffects":["The merchant quarter and the labourers' quarter remain walled apart"],"plotHooks":["A merchant is funding both the reform movement and the suppression of it"],"templateType":"economic_disparity","anchored":true}],"currentTensions":[{"type":"magical_controversy","description":"Debate over the role and regulation of magic divides the community","factions":["Pro-magic","Anti-magic","Regulation advocates"],"lastingEffects":["Spellcasting now requires a licence from the local authority","The site of the disputed working remains cordoned and warded"],"plotHooks":["A recent magical accident was covered up and the victims silenced","An anti-magic agitator is secretly using magic themselves","Something was sealed away using magic years ago and the seal is weakening"],"severity":["minor","major"]}],"historicalCharacter":"This place is older than the Tyranny, but people here date everything from it: before it, and after","eventsTimeline":[{"year":2,"yearsAgo":222,"name":"The Heresy Trials","type":"religious","anchored":false},{"year":77,"yearsAgo":147,"name":"The Wild Magic","type":"magical","anchored":false},{"year":108,"yearsAgo":116,"name":"The Siege","type":"disaster","anchored":true},{"year":114,"yearsAgo":110,"name":"The Purge","type":"occupation_infiltration","anchored":true},{"year":166,"yearsAgo":58,"name":"The Occupation","type":"exile_return","anchored":true},{"year":180,"yearsAgo":44,"name":"The Tyranny","type":"political","anchored":false},{"year":199,"yearsAgo":25,"name":"The Economic Divide","type":"economic","anchored":true}],"legacyAnnotations":[{"annotation":"As of the founding survey, the Tyranny (44 years ago) left trouble that has never been put right: the quarrel over who should rule today is the same quarrel, never settled.","eventType":"political","yearsAgo":44,"severity":"catastrophic","eventName":"The Tyranny"},{"annotation":"As of the founding survey, the Heresy Trials (222 years ago) set up ways of doing things that have since changed: the faith has lost much of its hold here since, and the settlement now runs its affairs with little say from the clergy.","eventType":"religious","yearsAgo":222,"severity":"minor","eventName":"The Heresy Trials"},{"annotation":"As of the founding survey, the Siege (116 years ago) hit the settlement hard, and it has since recovered: the changes made to get through that crisis are still how the place works today. What it left behind (a standing levy roster kept ready in the town archive) is still part of the place.","eventType":"disaster","yearsAgo":116,"severity":"major","eventName":"The Siege"}],"siegeNarrative":null},"isolationSupport":{"version":1,"applicable":false,"tier":"town","requiredCapacity":52,"capacity":52,"deficit":0,"status":"connected","paths":[],"magicDependent":false},"culturalIdentity":{"key":"norse","label":"Norse-inspired","scope":"Great halls and the sea, open assemblies, and a year planned around the hard season.","builtForm":"A compact hall-centered settlement stretches along the best shoreline, roadstead, or defensible ridge.","civicPattern":"Household leaders and law speakers bargain in assembly beneath a chieftain or royal representative.","exchangePattern":"Maritime trade, seasonal voyaging, fishing, pastoral production, and portable wealth drive exchange.","foodways":"Its own food is the day's catch. Smoking, drying, fermenting, and winter storage are central household technologies.","sacredLife":"Household rites, oath sites, burial memory, feast days, and formal sanctuaries overlap.","defensePattern":"Readily mobilized crews come first; ringworks, earth banks, and beacon systems follow where a place can man them.","socialTexture":"Law, household reputation, reciprocal gifts, and access to ships or land structure public standing.","architecturalDetail":"the assembly ground sits between the principal hall and the landing"},"culturalNotes":"Law, household reputation, reciprocal gifts, and access to ships or land structure public standing. A compact hall-centered settlement stretches along the best shoreline, roadstead, or defensible ridge.","stress":null,"stressors":null,"config":{"priorityEconomy":85,"priorityMilitary":23,"priorityReligion":29,"priorityCriminal":78,"settType":"town","population":1500,"tradeRouteAccess":"river","culture":"norse","contentProfile":"grounded","contentBoundaries":{"human_trafficking":false,"slavery":false,"torture":false,"hard_drugs":true},"settlementAgeMode":"auto","settlementAgeYears":0,"monsterThreat":"heartland","priorityMagic":43,"magicExists":true,"nearbyResourcesRandom":true,"nearbyResources":["river_fish","foraging_areas","hot_springs","stone_quarry","hunting_grounds"],"nearbyResourcesDepleted":["stone_quarry","hunting_g