":"Downstream/downwind","desc":"Smelly, dirty area with tanneries, butchers, and dyers","landmarks":["Tannery Row","Slaughterhouse","Dyer's Bridge"]},{"name":"Waterfront District","location":"Along the river","desc":"Warehouses, wharves, barges, dockworkers, and river traffic","landmarks":["Barge Wharf","Warehouse Row","River Landing"]},{"name":"Government Quarter","location":"Defensible high ground","desc":"Official buildings, courts, administrative offices","landmarks":["Town hall","Hireling hall","Courthouse"]}],"tradeAccess":"River access (water gate and docks)"},"availableServices":{"lodging":[{"name":"Accommodation","desc":"Beds from dormitory to private room. Quality varies by establishment.","institution":"Inn (multiple)"},{"name":"Lodging","desc":"Beds, meals, and stabling for travelers on the road. Priced by quality.","institution":"Coaching inn"},{"name":"Lodging (rooms to let)","desc":"A room let in a private house, by the night or the week.","institution":"Housing (75-650 households)"},{"name":"Short accommodation","desc":"Beds or floor space available in most taverns.","institution":"Taverns (5-20)"}],"food":[{"name":"Drink service","desc":"Ale, wine, and spirits across multiple establishments.","institution":"Taverns (5-20)"},{"name":"Fresh fish retail","desc":"Fish sold daily from the morning catch. Selection varies by season.","institution":"Fish market"},{"name":"Game meat","desc":"Venison, boar, rabbit. Seasonal and fresh.","institution":"Hunter's lodge"},{"name":"Grain grinding","desc":"Grind grain into flour for bread and other foods.","institution":"Mills (2-5)"}],"equipment":[{"name":"Barrel making","desc":"Watertight barrels for ale, wine, salted meat, and fish. Essential packaging for trade.","institution":"Cooper"},{"name":"Cask repair","desc":"Re-coopering and repair of used barrels. Cheaper than new for small leaks.","institution":"Cooper"},{"name":"Cloth production","desc":"Weave wool, linen, and other fibres into cloth for clothing and trade.","institution":"Weavers/Textile workers"},{"name":"Cut stone","desc":"Dressed stone blocks for construction. Consistency and size matter for fortifications.","institution":"Stone quarry"},{"name":"Fulled cloth","desc":"Washed and thickened cloth. Felted and durable.","institution":"Fuller"},{"name":"General trade","desc":"Agricultural produce, household goods, livestock. The economic heartbeat of the week.","institution":"Weekly market"},{"name":"Hide processing","desc":"Basic tanning of animal hides into usable leather.","institution":"Tanners"},{"name":"Livery and uniforms","desc":"House colours, guild uniforms, city watch livery.","institution":"Tailor's guild"},{"name":"Lumber milling","desc":"Raw logs into planks and beams. Essential input for all construction.","institution":"Sawmill (commercial)"},{"name":"Rubble and aggregate","desc":"Rough stone for road beds and fill. Bulk sale, low value per unit.","institution":"Stone quarry"},{"name":"Salt production","desc":"Evaporation, boiling, or mining to produce raw salt. Essential preservative.","institution":"Salt works"},{"name":"Seasonal trading","desc":"Once-a-year market drawing merchants from across the region.","institution":"Annual fair"},{"name":"Shoe repair","desc":"Full guild workshop. Any repair.","institution":"Cobbler's guild"},{"name":"Standard boots","desc":"Guild-certified boots. Quality-marked, price-regulated.","institution":"Cobbler's guild"},{"name":"Weekly market","desc":"Regular market days with produce, goods, and livestock.","institution":"Market square"},{"name":"Working clothes (bulk)","desc":"Practical clothing for soldiers and servants.","institution":"Tailor's guild"}],"magic":[{"name":"Potion brewing","desc":"Healing potions, antidotes, and alchemical compounds on request.","institution":"Alchemist shop"}],"information":[{"name":"Message relay","desc":"Pass dispatches and letters along the relay chain. Fresh horses at each station.","institution":"Post relay station"},{"name":"Register of the dead","desc":"The sexton records who lies where. Consulted in inheritance disputes as often as in mourning.","institution":"Parish burial grounds"}],"healing":[{"name":"Burial","desc":"Interment in the congregation's ground, with the rite that congregation keeps.","institution":"Parish burial grounds"},{"name":"Herbal remedies","desc":"Tinctures, poultices, and dried herbs for common ailments.","institution":"Apothecary (established)"},{"name":"Life ceremonies","desc":"Births, marriages, and funerals across several congregations.","institution":"Parish churches (2-5)"},{"name":"Medicines and compounds","desc":"Prepared medicines for fever, pain, infection, and chronic conditions.","institution":"Apothecary (established)"},{"name":"Religious services","desc":"Several congregations covering different districts or communities.","institution":"Parish churches (2-5)"}],"transport":[{"name":"Barge construction","desc":"Flat-bottomed cargo barges for river transport. Simpler than sea vessels.","institution":"River boatyard"},{"name":"Boat repair","desc":"Hull patching, oar replacement, caulking. River traffic takes constant punishment.","institution":"River boatyard"},{"name":"Cargo freight","desc":"Bulk cargo transport along navigable rivers. Grain, stone, timber, goods.","institution":"Barge and river transport company"},{"name":"Horse hire","desc":"Rent horses for single journeys or extended travel. Quality varies by price.","institution":"Stable district"},{"name":"Livery and boarding","desc":"Board privately owned horses. Feed, care, and exercise included.","institution":"Stable district"},{"name":"River crossing","desc":"Transport foot travelers and small goods across the river.","institution":"River ferry"},{"name":"Vessel mooring","desc":"Berth assignment and dock fees. Main revenue of port administration.","institution":"Docks/port facilities"}],"legal":[{"name":"Bylaws and ordinances","desc":"Enacts and enforces the town's own rules","institution":"Town council"},{"name":"Cargo loading and unloading","desc":"Longshoremen and crane equipment for shifting goods between ship and shore.","institution":"Docks/port facilities"},{"name":"Civic announcements","desc":"Official proclamations, wanted notices, and public notices read in the square.","institution":"Market square"},{"name":"Civil disputes","desc":"Settle contract/property issues","institution":"Courthouse"},{"name":"Criminal trials","desc":"Judge crimes","institution":"Courthouse"},{"name":"Dispute adjudication","desc":"Hears the town's civil pleas at the council bench","institution":"Town council"},{"name":"Dispute arbitration","desc":"Bring commercial and civil disputes before a magistrate.","institution":"Town hall"},{"name":"Goods storage","desc":"Secure, dry storage for trade goods awaiting sale or onward shipment.","institution":"Merchant warehouses"},{"name":"Grain storage","desc":"Municipal grain reserves. Buffers the settlement against poor harvests.","institution":"Town granary"},{"name":"Market charter and tolls","desc":"Grants stalls, sets tolls, licenses the market","institution":"Town council"},{"name":"Night patrol","desc":"Patrol the streets after dark. Deter crime and respond to incidents.","institution":"Town watch"},{"name":"Permit applications","desc":"Apply for construction, business, and trade permits.","institution":"Town hall"},{"name":"Quality certification","desc":"Guild mark indicating goods meet agreed standards.","institution":"Craft guilds (5-15)"},{"name":"Tax payment","desc":"Pay annual and quarterly taxes and levies.","institution":"Town hall"},{"name":"Trade brokerage","desc":"Facilitate large commercial transactions between distant parties.","institution":"Merchant guilds (3-8)"}],"employment":[{"name":"Animal training","desc":"Train animals for specific purposes: guard, hunt, war, labour, entertainment.","institution":"Beast trainers"},{"name":"Apprenticeship programs","desc":"Formal training under a master craftsperson. Multi-year commitment.","institution":"Craft guilds (5-15)"},{"name":"Hunting guide hire","desc":"A tracker who knows the territory.","institution":"Hunter's lodge"},{"name":"Laborer hire","desc":"Unskilled and semi-skilled laborers for day work.","institution":"Hireling hall"},{"name":"Specialist hire","desc":"Skilled trades and specialist workers for contract periods.","institution":"Hireling hall"}],"entertainment":[{"name":"Betting","desc":"Wager on fight outcomes. House takes a cut.","institution":"Fighting pits"},{"name":"Cold reading","desc":"Convincing but fraudulent personality readings.","institution":"Charlatan fortune tellers"},{"name":"Combat entertainment","desc":"Unarmed or armed fights for crowd entertainment. Stakes and rules vary.","institution":"Fighting pits"}],"criminal":[{"name":"Contraband licensing","desc":"Those who run the crime here decide what moves through. Anyone who moves goods without their leave is removed.","institution":"(criminal governance)"},{"name":"Dispute resolution (criminal)","desc":"Quarrels are settled by those who run the crime here. Their judgment is final, and resisting it is unwise.","institution":"(criminal governance)"},{"name":"Extortion (structured)","desc":"The rate is posted. Everyone pays. It is not officially called extortion.","institution":"(criminal governance)"},{"name":"Front company formation","desc":"Establish a legitimate face for work that needs to look above board.","institution":"(commercial crime)"},{"name":"Gray market goods","desc":"Legitimately produced goods moving through channels that avoid inspection, duty, or guild oversight.","institution":"(commercial crime)"},{"name":"Petty crime","desc":"Pickpocketing, muggings, and opportunistic theft in their territory.","institution":"Street gang"},{"name":"Unofficial arbitration","desc":"Commercial disputes resolved outside the courts: faster, cheaper, and more reliably enforced.","institution":"(commercial crime)"}]},"powerStructure":{"factions":[{"faction":"Merchant Council","modifier":"commerce-driven","power":32,"desc":"Merchant interests dominate the council; trade policy is the primary concern. The craft guilds are present but outpaced; merchants set prices, craft masters object, and merchants win more often than not. They tolerate the guild's cut because fighting it costs more than paying it, and nobody says so aloud.","isGoverning":true,"category":"economy","rawPower":35,"powerLabel":"Strong","captureState":"equilibrium"},{"faction":"Merchant Guilds","power":31,"desc":"The ruling class and the merchant class are the same people; commercial decisions are political decisions and civic access is purchased. The gap between them and the governing council is narrow. A single shift in patronage, scandal, or armed muscle could swap their positions. The craft guilds are present but outpaced; merchants set prices, craft masters object, and merchants win more often than not. They tolerate the guild's cut because fighting it costs more than paying it, and nobody says so aloud.","category":"economy","rawPower":28,"powerLabel":"Strong"},{"faction":"Thieves' Guild","power":22,"desc":"Underworld effectively controls vice and key officials; the seat is stronger, but has not moved to break its hold. Close enough to the two above that their support is worth buying; they play Merchant Guilds and Merchant Council against each other when they can.","category":"criminal","rawPower":17,"powerLabel":"Significant"},{"faction":"Craft Guilds","power":15,"desc":"The trades regulate their own production and apprenticeships; a reliable secondary presence in civic life. The merchants consistently outvote them on pricing and labour standards, so craft masters now win what they can by adding their own conditions to each deal.","category":"economy","rawPower":14,"powerLabel":"Minor"}],"governingName":"Merchant Council","government":"Merchant Council","stability":"Unstable — criminal governance","recentConflict":"The guild and the district council both claim authority over the new market. Violence has settled some of the disputes; more is expected.","publicLegitimacy":{"score":36,"label":"Contested","color":"#8a4010","bg":"#fdf6ec","breakdown":{"prosperity":8,"safety":-20,"defense":-2,"food":0},"govMultiplier":0.8,"crimMultiplier":1.15,"isEndorsed":false,"isApproved":false,"isTolerated":false,"isContested":true,"isLegitimacyCrisis":false,"governanceFractured":false},"factionRelationships":[{"pair":["Merchant Council","Merchant Guilds"],"type":"dependent","direction":"stable","ratio":1,"narrative":"Merchant Council needs the taxes and loans of Merchant Guilds, and Merchant Guilds need Merchant Council to enforce their contracts and keep the law. Neither can afford to ruin the other."},{"pair":["Merchant Council","Thieves' Guild"],"type":"tense","direction":"stable","captureState":"equilibrium","narrative":"Merchant Council leaves Thieves' Guild alone because stamping it out would cost more than it saves. Thieves' Guild keeps its head down, because it needs the hall standing to feed off it.","dmNote":"Ask: which specific officials have arrangements with Thieves' Guild? The answer drives dozens of plot hooks."},{"pair":["Merchant Guilds","Craft Guilds"],"type":"competitive","direction":"stable","ratio":2.07,"narrative":"Merchant Guilds buy the materials, set the prices and sell the goods; Craft Guilds only make them, and their masters are becoming hired hands in all but name."}],"criminalCaptureState":"equilibrium","powerProjectionVersion":1,"economyInputFingerprint":"power-economy-v1:dc68601b","conflicts":[{"parties":["Merchant Council","Craft Guilds"],"issue":"Military conscription of guild apprentices","stakes":"Labor control","intensity":"high","desc":"Merchant Council and Craft Guilds are in high conflict over military conscription of guild apprentices. The stakes are labor control. It reaches Merchant Guilds too, who are not a party to it.","plotHooks":["Leading members of both powers are partners in the same business, one that skirts the law, and neither side wants that said aloud during arbitration."]}]},"settlementReason":["Sited at the water's edge, where the river was the only road worth having, and it has been the argument for staying ever since."],"npcs":[{"id":"npc_merchant_guilds_3_8","name":"Freya Ljotsson","gender":"female","role":"Burgomaster","title":"the senior guild master","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"greedy","modifier":"cautious","tell":"quotes scripture or proverbs in casual conversation","speech":"Peppers speech with trade or craft jargon even in unrelated contexts"},"physical":{"age":"mid-twenties","build":"willowy","feature":"a voice that carries further than intended","clothes":"clothes that once cost a fortune and now show the miles"},"goal":{"short":"Make sure every decision of Merchant Council this season goes out under their own name.","long":"Make Drifa Andersson the first of many who owe them.","intent":{"short":{"family":"RANK","kind":"defend","key":"consolidate_power","target":{"kind":"npc","id":"npc_docks_port_facilities"}},"long":{"family":"TIES","kind":"creditor","key":"collect_debt","target":{"kind":"npc","id":"npc_inn_multiple"}}}},"secret":{"what":"Secretly receives what they believe are genuine divine visions, which terrifies them","stakes":"Acting on the visions would be seen as madness; ignoring them may be worse"},"plotHooks":["They have promised the same order to two buyers, and both are due to collect on the same morning."],"influence":"high","power":8,"presentation":{"impression":"Cautious with newcomers, because the work requires it; it is nothing personal.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Says little until it is clear what you can offer."},"institution":{"kind":"house","key":"Merchant guilds (3-8)","family":"Merchant guilds (3-8)","title":"the senior guild master","veiled":false},"memberships":[{"power":"Merchant Council","rank":1,"share":1,"veiled":false}],"importance":"pillar","structuralPosition":"Holds the seat, but many doubt its right to it, and the doubt has not gone away. Still the senior guild master as well.","activeConstraint":"Every hard move gives the doubters a new reason; every delay lets the doubt grow.","settlementCondition":"contested","structuralRank":"head"},{"id":"npc_barge_and_river_transport_company","name":"Ulfric Snorrason","gender":"male","role":"the barge master","title":"the barge master","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"vengeful","modifier":"traditionalist","tell":"drums fingers on surfaces when thinking","speech":"Quotes their own past pronouncements as though citing law"},"physical":{"age":"early forties","build":"willowy","feature":"an old injury that affects their gait","clothes":"well-cut but understated trading clothes"},"goal":{"short":"Do Auðr Snorrason one useful favour this season, unasked.","long":"Turn the contest with Craft Guilds into a partnership on terms set by Merchant Guilds.","intent":{"short":{"family":"TIES","kind":"ally","key":"protect_ally","target":{"kind":"npc","id":"npc_coaching_inn"}},"long":{"family":"POWER","kind":"competitive","key":"expand_influence","target":{"kind":"power","id":"Craft Guilds"}}}},"secret":{"what":"Has been overloading the barges, and one sank last season with a crew aboard","stakes":"The families of the drowned want someone to blame, and the loading tallies are still on file"},"plotHooks":["A young trader has been undercutting them in ways that shouldn't be possible on their claimed capital."],"influence":"low","power":1,"presentation":{"impression":"Watches the cargo and the people near it.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Asks what you are sending and where; writes it down."},"institution":{"kind":"house","key":"Barge and river transport company","family":"Barge and river transport company","title":"the barge master","veiled":false},"memberships":[{"power":"Merchant Guilds","rank":1,"share":1,"veiled":false}],"importance":"pillar","structuralPosition":"Heads the leading house in the trade while many doubt the seat's right; whatever the seat does next can make or break it.","activeConstraint":"Keeping friends on both sides means neither side fully trusts the house.","settlementCondition":"contested","structuralRank":"head"},{"id":"npc_craft_guilds_5_15","name":"Rorik Mordsson","gender":"male","role":"the senior craft-guild master","title":"the senior craft-guild master","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"paranoid","modifier":"idealistic","tell":"taps their foot in a complex rhythm when bored","speech":"Refers to past events as though they're common knowledge"},"physical":{"age":"early twenties","build":"willowy","feature":"laugh lines that run deep","clothes":"sober broadcloth with buttons worth more than the coat"},"goal":{"short":"Find out what Kjara Eindriðason really wants in return.","long":"Leave Merchant Guilds holding nothing that Craft Guilds could not take away.","intent":{"short":{"family":"TIES","kind":"debtor","key":"repay_debt","target":{"kind":"npc","id":"npc_weavers_textile_workers"}},"long":{"family":"POWER","kind":"competitive","key":"expand_influence","target":{"kind":"power","id":"Merchant Guilds"}}}},"secret":{"what":"Has been falsifying inspection records for a fee","stakes":"The next disaster caused by the uninspected goods will be traced back to them"},"plotHooks":["A crate came to them by mistake, and the people who meant to receive it have started asking around for it."],"influence":"low","power":1,"presentation":{"impression":"Quick to smile, quick to calculate. Both things are happening simultaneously.","disposition":"welcoming","behaviour":"Friendly on the surface, but soon asks where you are staying and who sent you."},"institution":{"kind":"house","key":"Craft guilds (5-15)","family":"Craft guilds (5-15)","title":"the senior craft-guild master","veiled":false},"memberships":[{"power":"Craft Guilds","rank":1,"share":1,"veiled":false}],"importance":"pillar","structuralPosition":"Runs a smaller house that sells to the seat's people and to its doubters alike.","activeConstraint":"To both sides, staying out of it looks like fear or scheming.","settlementCondition":"contested","structuralRank":"head"},{"id":"npc_veiled_e01881c4d24ae7e3","name":"Jarl Asgautsson","gender":"male","role":"the gang boss","title":"the gang boss","category":"criminal","personality":{"dominant":"incorruptible","flaw":"mendacious","modifier":"opportunistic","tell":"never eats or drinks anything offered by a stranger without watching others first","speech":"Trails off mid-sentence when approaching something they regret knowing"},"physical":{"age":"mid-fifties","build":"lean and wiry","feature":"teeth that have been replaced with metal","clothes":"good boots and cheap everything else"},"goal":{"short":"Win one ally of Merchant Council over to the side of Thieves' Guild.","long":"Pull the strings in this place without anyone seeing their hand.","intent":{"short":{"family":"POWER","kind":"tense","key":"expand_influence","target":{"kind":"power","id":"Merchant Council"}},"long":{"family":"PERSONALITY","kind":"forbidden_patron","key":"indulge_trait","target":null}}},"secret":{"what":"Knows something about Inga Bodvarsson that Inga Bodvarsson believes no one else knows, and has been deciding for months whether to use it","stakes":"Inga Bodvarsson would move against them immediately if they suspected"},"plotHooks":["An honest official they have never managed to buy has started asking about one of their fronts by name."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Lean, quiet and watchful. People on the street step aside without being asked.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Asks who you are and who you know; strangers are tolerated, not welcomed."},"institution":{"kind":"house","key":"Street gang","family":"Multiple criminal factions","title":"the gang boss","veiled":true},"memberships":[{"power":"Thieves' Guild","rank":1,"share":1,"veiled":true}],"importance":"pillar","structuralPosition":"Heads the crew while many doubt the seat's right and those who keep order look elsewhere.","activeConstraint":"The seat may turn on the crew to show it can still keep order, so today's freedom could end without warning.","settlementCondition":"contested","structuralRank":"head"},{"id":"npc_stone_quarry","name":"Geira Snorrason","gender":"female","role":"the quarry master","title":"the quarry master","category":"economy","personality":{"dominant":null,"flaw":"callous","modifier":"hedonistic","tell":"cleans or fidgets with their hands constantly","speech":"Swears colourfully but apologises immediately after"},"physical":{"age":"early sixties","build":"slight: smaller than expected for the role","feature":"surprisingly soft hands","clothes":"clothes that once cost a fortune and now show the miles"},"goal":{"short":"Take one piece of business from Craft Guilds and bring it to Merchant Guilds.","long":"Make the stone quarry so needed by those who govern that no one dares touch the rights of the house.","intent":{"short":{"family":"POWER","kind":"competitive","key":"expand_influence","target":{"kind":"power","id":"Craft Guilds"}},"long":{"family":"INSTITUTION","kind":"charter","key":"control_institution","target":{"kind":"house","id":"Stone quarry"}}}},"secret":{"what":"Sold flawed stone for a building that is now cracking, and swore it was sound","stakes":"When the building comes down, the quarry's mark will be found on the blocks"},"plotHooks":["A buyer has paid them in advance for a whole season of goods, far above the price, and will not say what the goods are for."],"influence":"low","power":3,"presentation":{"impression":"Watches the quarry face and the workers more than the visitor.","disposition":"cautious","behaviour":"Answers questions about the stone; questions about the accidents are turned aside."},"institution":{"kind":"house","key":"Stone quarry","family":"Stone quarry","ti